# Does an OZ spending_limit BIND beside our interpreter?
# Generated 2026-08-22T18:29:53Z by packages/policy-synth/scripts/oz-spending-limit-binding.ts
#
# `oz-policy-composition.log` settled the composition RULE (all-of) using two
# instances of OUR OWN interpreter. This settles the remaining question: does a
# REAL third-party policy stop a call our interpreter permits?
#
# One rule shape throughout, one variable - the extra policy:
#   rule 1  CONTROL  interpreter only
#   rule 2  SUBJECT  interpreter + OZ spending_limit(cap 5000000 stroops)
#
# Three calls, each load-bearing:
#   1. CONTROL over-cap  -> must PASS  (attributes any deny to the cap alone)
#   2. SUBJECT under-cap -> must PASS  (the rule is a bound, not a brick)
#   3. SUBJECT over-cap  -> must DENY #3221 SpendingLimitExceeded
#
# The spending_limit contracts are OZ example code we built from tag v0.7.2 and
# deployed ourselves. We did not audit it; see docs/audit/README.md for the
# provenance note.

